Reference-free 2-df SAMPLE_RACE block LR test: 41.44 (p=1.0e-9) unadjusted -> 25.59 (p=2.8e-6) with SES
-> 1.54 (p=0.46) with SES+ACADEMIC -> 4.82 (p=0.090) with SES+ACADEMIC+famsize. Never returns to
significance in the fully adjusted model. SAMPLE_SEX 1-df: p=0.124 -> 0.092, never significant.
Which academic variable does it: +ABILITY only -> race NS (p=0.37); +PERCENTILE only -> race still
significant (p=0.002). So the test-score composite is the active mediator.

## Reproduction of 0.5024 -> 0.0923
Not reproduced exactly by any of ~1,000 focal x specification x family x scaling combinations
(best absolute error 0.038). Closest scale-consistent match: SAMPLE_RACE (White vs non-White) in the
standardised-predictor logit, 0.4752 -> 0.0362 (p=0.68); ordinal race coding gives 0.4776 -> -0.0041.
FAMILY SIZE's raw logit (-0.5077) matches the 0.5024 magnitude by coincidence but shows zero attenuation.
The conclusion therefore rests on the attenuation/shrinkage pattern (~82–99% attenuation with loss of
significance, unique to SAMPLE_RACE), as agreed.

## Event-sparsity verdict
Firth penalised logistic on the fully adjusted model reproduces the MLE to <1e-6 for every coefficient
(no separation). SEs rise only 7–10% from M0 to M3 while race coefficients move 0.9–1.3 log-odds:
the loss of significance is a genuine change in the point estimate, not 236-event sparsity. Caveat stands
that only 28 Black and 19 Hispanic BA completers exist, so race-cell CIs are wide.

